    {
      "id": "claim_bea3fbc5095e4637ab1f06a5a195012d",
      "statement": "Local/dynamic pool start registers shared rules on existing slots including draining slots before starting the stable listener and requesting growth, with rollback on failure. Admission selects registered non-draining slots by lowest reported per-rule count and round-robin ties; Remote starts on the primary only. The standalone runner starts the rule and waits up to 120 seconds for the effective pool size before workload time/CPU sampling, forcing one for Remote; auxiliary opening/installation is limited to four concurrent slots and registration precedes admission. Metrics exclude cold expansion and report the final connected count. Its timed matrix covers request/response, duplex, jumps, mixed workloads, and separately reported five-second idle CPU; slow-consumer and listener/disconnect lifecycle cases remain functional wire coverage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Benchmarks/PortForwarding/main.swift#L135-L270",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b52a6d9ed10f664ca3ab86013fd83397fc0ce8c4034f65452f6d0ff734cfd898:"
